{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779051158,"nonce":"bk1jxBNut77QQHOCoVY0RHHMQPw=","message":"Implementation status for `feature/feedbax-execution-contract`:\n\n- Added a provider-neutral `ExecutionSpec` / `ExecutionPlan` model for `local`, `ssh`, `runpod`, and `modal` backends.\n- Modeled RunPod as pod allocation plus the shared SSH worker contract, with current defaults from recent RLRMP practice: `/workspace`, 30 GB container/volume defaults, 5090/4090 preference, SSH readiness, `runpodctl pod create` preview, and explicit `pid` / `exit_code` / `done` sentinels.\n- Modeled Modal separately as image/function/volume/secret execution, including generated Modal app rendering and `map`/`spawn_map` cell submission. GitHub refs become image requirements so dev use can require a pushed ref instead of local rsync.\n- Kept local execution executable now: `feedbax-provider run-local` runs an explicitly local spec, writes logs and an execution plan, and emits a durable training manifest with provenance.\n- Exposed execution planning through provider manifest schemas/capabilities, CLI (`execution-plan`, `run-local`, `modal-app`), and HTTP (`POST /api/provider/execution/plan`).\n\nCurrent official-doc checks used for the adapter surface:\n- RunPod REST pod creation documents `gpuTypeIds`, `ports`, `volumeInGb`, `containerDiskInGb`, and `volumeMountPath`: https://docs.runpod.io/api-reference/pods/POST/pods\n- `runpodctl pod create` exposes the corresponding image/GPU/disk/volume/ports/cloud flags and SSH enablement: https://docs.runpod.io/runpodctl/reference/runpodctl-pod\n- Modal batch processing documents `.spawn_map` for detached asynchronous jobs and `.map` for gathered parallel results: https://modal.com/docs/guide/batch-processing\n- Modal Volumes require explicit `commit()` for writes to become visible outside the current container: https://modal.com/docs/guide/volumes\n- Modal GPU docs support fallback GPU lists and single-node multi-GPU syntax: https://modal.com/docs/guide/gpu\n\nVerification so far:\n- `uv run pytest tests/test_execution_contract.py tests/test_provider_contract.py` passed.\n- `uv run ruff check feedbax/execution.py feedbax/provider.py feedbax/bin/provider.py feedbax/web/api/provider.py tests/test_execution_contract.py` passed.\n- A generated Modal app from a sample spec compiles with `python -m py_compile`.\n\nOut of scope for this commit: live cloud credential use or spending. The live RunPod/Modal submitters should sit on top of the generated plan/app surface rather than bypass it.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}